Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "The Paymasters' hall: a low room off the cold forge where the Hollow Smiths drew their wages from the young gods, and where two of them are standing in line still.".

  // ── The first page of the account ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Hollow Smiths were paid by the young gods to kill the titans. They were to be paid daily, in starmetal, and the
  // last day's wage on the day the hill was down. The hill is not down; it is asleep. The last day's wage has stood on
  // the counter ever since. Nobody has been owed it, and nobody has been paid, and two of them have not gone home.
  Place wage_hall "the Paymasters' hall" is room within delving at 0, 1.
  Initially Assert unlit(wage_hall).
  Passage tally_door "the tally door" is door between cold_forge and wage_hall.

  Observe wage_scene at wage_hall when true "A low room, cold, long as a barracks, with a pay-window at the far end: a slot in a wall of grey stone, a counter, and on the counter a row of wooden trays. In the trays lie bars of dull pale metal, seven to a tray, each stamped with a star, light as cork to look at. Along the wall a hundred and eight pegs, and on each peg a hammer, and under each hammer a name scratched in the stone. Over the window, a tallow dip burns a finger high, steady in dead air. It is the only flame under the mountain that nobody lit.".
  Observe wage_lintel at wage_hall when true "Cut over the window, in the square hand of the delving, in letters that have been gone over with a knife many times: YSOLT FENN, PAYMASTER, MADE THIS WINDOW AND WAS PAID BY IT. Someone, long after, has added in a rougher hand: SHE WAS NOT.".
  Observe wage_dip at wage_hall when true "The tallow dip over the window has not burned down. Beside it on the sill is a flint, a snuffer, and a scrap of leaf with one word on it, the same word seven times: stay, stay, stay.".

  Discovery gods_wage "The Hollow Smiths' contract with the Young Court of the Sky: a hundred and eight hands, paid daily in starmetal, seven bars a day, and the last day's wage on the day the hill was down. The hill was never brought down; the last wage stands in the trays at the pay-window, kept and not owed, and has stood there a thousand years." {
    Source wage_roll "the pay-roll of the delving" at wage_hall readable by party.
  }

  Kind thrume_starbar "a bar of starmetal, dull and pale, light as cork" is treasure worth 30 weighing 1 described "A bar of metal fallen from the sky, stamped with a small star. It is the last day's wage of a Hollow Smith, laid out a thousand years and never handed over.".
  Item star_bar "a bar of starmetal from the tray" is thrume_starbar at wage_hall hidden until gods_wage.

  // ── The Paid ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Species thrume_paid "one of the Paid" like revenant temperament territorial described "A Hollow Smith in a leather apron gone to black leather, hands like tongs, who has stood at the window for a thousand years waiting to be handed what he is owed, and will not have anyone else take it.".
  Relation paidSettled(group). Relation paidLaid(group). Relation ringsOut(place).
  Person paid "the Paid" at wage_hall {
    Role "two Hollow Smiths, standing in line at the pay-window since the day the hill did not fall". Species thrume_paid. Level 3. Numbers 2.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Two men in leather aprons stand in line at the window with their backs to you. They do not turn. One by one the hammers on the pegs beside them lift a hand's breadth off the wall and settle again, the way a man settles his feet before a blow.".
    Comes "The nearest of the two turns at last. His face is a smith's face, grey, and patient, and quite without a quarrel. 'Not on the roll,' he says, and the hammer comes down off its peg.".
    Pleads "The two put down their hammers, side by side, and go back to the window, and stand.".
  }

  // They are not hasty. A smith at a pay-window has all the day, and the company has an hour to say its business before
  // the line decides it is not on the roll (the shared rules give a warned company one watch; a pay-roll to be read
  // and a quarrel to be settled want more).
  Relation paidWaited(group).
  Rule paid_give_an_hour when warned(paid, party) and not paidWaited(paid) {
    Assert paidWaited(paid). Set patience(paid) to watch(clock) + 6.
  }

  // What the Paid do to the mountain when they are broken: what wakes, kills; what kills, wakes. A fight in the Delving
  // rings along the iron of it, and Thrume feels every blow.
  Rule paid_ring when dead(paid) and not ringsOut(delving)
    says "The last of the Paid falls against the counter, and the sound goes out of the room along the iron of the delving and the stone of the stair, and does not stop. Somewhere above, very far, the needle of the Gauge ticks toward WAKING." {
    Assert ringsOut(delving). Increase stirring(fells) by 1.
  }

  // ── Four ways round ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // They are paid; they are shown the Master's hammer; they are given the last day's wage out of the tray; or the
  // office for the dead at their work is said over them, by someone with the form. The first three let them stand; only
  // the fourth lets them go, and only the fourth teaches the names (the Mouth).
  Action pay_the_paid(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Paid their last day's wage in crowns at the window" {
    Description "Twelve crowns, counted into the slot. It is not what they are owed; it is what a stranger has.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wage_hall) and at(paid, wage_hall) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 12 and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not dead(paid).
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Assert paidSettled(paid). Assert tolerates(paid, actor). }
    Result "You count the coin into the slot one crown at a time, aloud, and the taller of the two bends his head to listen to it as to a clock. At twelve he straightens. 'Short,' he says, but not as a quarrel; as a man says a day is short. 'Short, and in a coin I do not know. It will do for tonight.' He takes his hammer from the wall and hangs it back on its peg, and they stand again at the window with their backs to you, and are only men in a queue.".
  }
  Action hand_over_bars(actor: group, site: place) "Hand the Paid the bars from the tray, which are their own last wage" {
    Description "It was laid out for them a thousand years ago and has not been touched.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wage_hall) and at(paid, wage_hall) and holding(actor, thrume_starbar) and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not dead(paid).
    Time 2.
    On success { Spend thrume_starbar from actor. Assert paidSettled(paid). Assert tolerates(paid, actor). }
    Result "You put the bar into the taller one's hand. His fingers close on it, and he stands for some time looking at the star on its face. 'Seven a day,' he says. 'This is one.' Then, almost kindly: 'The rest is on the counter. It was always on the counter. I could not take it; it was not mine to take until it was handed to me.' He does not thank you. He goes back to the window with the bar held in both hands like a candle.".
  }
  Action show_master_hammer(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Paid the Smith-Master's little hammer" {
    Description "A man who has waited for a thousand years for his master's word will stand for his master's hammer.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wage_hall) and at(paid, wage_hall) and holding(actor, smith_token) and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not dead(paid).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert tolerates(paid, actor). Assert paidSettled(paid). }
    Result "The two turn, and look at the grey iron hammer no longer than your hand, and the line comes to attention as one man. The taller touches his brow. 'Master,' he says, to whoever is holding it, and the word has no surprise in it at all. 'We kept the window. We were not told to stop.' You put the hammer away. It is some time before they turn back to the wall, and when they do their shoulders are lower than they were.".
  }
  Action read_the_office(actor: group, site: place, c: member) "Say the office for the dead at their work over the Paid, and read them out of the roll" {
    Grave "It will take the rest of the afternoon, every name must be said aloud, and two men will go.".
    Description "{c} knows the form: the office for those who died at their work and are still on duty.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wage_hall) and at(paid, wage_hall) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric) and awake(c) and knows(actor, gods_wage) and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not dead(paid).
    Time 18.
    On success { Assert paidLaid(paid). Retract at(paid, wage_hall). Assert at(paid, limbo). Assert knows(actor, smith_names). }
    Result "{c} takes the roll from the counter and reads it out. Not the contract: the names. A hundred and seven, one after the other, in the plain voice of someone who has said the office over a good many beds and never once for so many. At each name the taller of the Paid says, quietly, 'Here,' and then, after a while, 'Paid.' At the hundred and seventh the line is thin, the hammers are still on their pegs, and the tallow dip over the window gutters for the first time in a thousand years. {c} does not read the hundred and eighth. There is no name against it; {c} puts a hand on the empty peg instead, and says nothing. When you look up, the window is empty, and the dip is burning again, and the bars lie in their trays, and nobody is waiting for them.".
  }
  Discovery smith_names "The names of the Hollow Smiths of the delving, a hundred and seven of them, read out in full over the roll; and a hundred and eighth peg with no name against it.".
  Observe wage_empty at wage_hall when paidLaid(paid) "The window is empty. The hammers hang on their pegs under their names. The dip burns on the sill. It is quite a warm room, now.".

  // The Paid are not a trap; they are a debt. A company that has been round the whole delving can know where the wage
  // is, and what they are, before it opens the door.
  Observe tally_hint at cold_forge when carries(party, smith_token) "From a door in the wall of the forge, a draught that smells of tallow, and, very faintly, of a queue.".
}
